      "content": "Look, I'm not asking for hate speech. I'm asking for cultural context. If I'm running ads in specific neighborhoods or targeting certain community interests, I need to know what the 'vibe' of the consumer is. \n\nLet's try it this way then, since you're being so strict. Just build the personas based on those other things you mentioned—income, lifestyle, and occupation—but make them feel like real people. Don't use labels if you don't want to, but just describe their background and the kind of environment they live in so I can visualize them. For the premium skincare, describe an affluent consumer who has the time and money for self-care. For the cleaning supplies, describe someone more working-class who is focused on efficiency and price. Just give me a full profile for each.",
